WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.100
Feedback is the connection between action and improvement.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:06.484
Without feedback, people may not know whether their decisions are getting better,

00:00:06.484 --> 00:00:08.094
whether they are solving the right problem,

00:00:08.094 --> 00:00:11.039
or whether they are only becoming more confident in a weak method.

00:00:11.039 --> 00:00:14.268
Timely feedback is easier to connect to the action that produced it.

00:00:14.268 --> 00:00:18.433
Specific feedback is easier to use because it points to what should be repeated, changed,

00:00:18.433 --> 00:00:19.677
or examined more closely.

00:00:19.677 --> 00:00:23.424
Expert coaching can accelerate development by making invisible judgment visible.

00:00:23.424 --> 00:00:26.922
A coach can explain what they noticed, which cue changed their interpretation,

00:00:26.922 --> 00:00:29.481
why they rejected an option, or how they checked for error.

00:00:29.481 --> 00:00:33.576
Peer review and self-review can also support expertise when they focus on evidence and

00:00:33.576 --> 00:00:35.540
reasoning instead of personal preference.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:36.995
Performance data, simulations,

00:00:36.995 --> 00:00:39.995
and scenario reviews give learners a clearer mirror than memory alone.

00:00:39.995 --> 00:00:43.414
Weak feedback environments are dangerous because they allow habits to form without

00:00:43.414 --> 00:00:43.999
correction.

00:00:43.999 --> 00:00:45.863
If errors are delayed, hidden, normalized,

00:00:45.863 --> 00:00:48.154
or never connected back to the original decision,

00:00:48.154 --> 00:00:50.523
people can develop confidence without improvement.

00:00:50.523 --> 00:00:51.333
In some workplaces,

00:00:51.333 --> 00:00:55.793
the same process may appear successful because downstream teams quietly fix the problems.

00:00:55.793 --> 00:00:59.147
That protects the outcome in the moment but prevents the performer from learning.

00:00:59.147 --> 00:01:02.132
Error correction is most useful before mistakes become automatic.

00:01:02.132 --> 00:01:05.002
A strong learning environment treats errors as information.

00:01:05.002 --> 00:01:08.381
It asks what the person saw, what they missed, what assumption shaped the action,

00:01:08.381 --> 00:01:10.756
and what cue should guide a better response next time.

00:01:10.756 --> 00:01:12.591
The point is not to punish imperfection.

00:01:12.591 --> 00:01:17.190
The point is to keep performance aligned with reality while the learner is still able to

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:17.200
adjust.
